From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:08:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: honour CMD_UMS_ABORT_KEYED
 while idle

While no command is pending, the gadget waits in sleep_thread(), where
ctrlc() takes and drops any other key. With CMD_UMS_ABORT_KEYED, ums
then only noticed a key that arrived while a SCSI command was handled.
Check for any key there as well.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
index 76ee08dc5e8..d41a88db2d2 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
@@ -669,7 +669,11 @@ static int sleep_thread(struct fsg_common *common)
 			if (common->eject)
 				return -EPIPE;
 
-			/* Handle CTRL+C */
+			/* Handle CTRL+C, or any key with CMD_UMS_ABORT_KEYED */
+			if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMD_UMS_ABORT_KEYED) && tstc()) {
+				getchar();
+				return -EPIPE;
+			}
 			if (ctrlc())
 				return -EPIPE;
 
